Reading it: `decl-ctrl` is the point — the share of never-written questions
the floor declines instead of answering with the nearest-looking thing.
`decl-ans` is what that restraint costs on real questions, and R@5 is what
survives after the trim. The shipped floor should sit where decl-ctrl is
high, decl-ans is negligible, and R@5 has not moved.

